    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Atomic: plane seed + in-memory video-tracking into plane_quad.v1\r\n(persist_to_file=false, no draft copy).\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h, --help                            Print this help message and exit\r\n      --ref TEXT                        Draft ref (standalone in-memory session; optional when the host\r\n                                        supplies an external editor session).\r\n      --target-seg-id TEXT REQUIRED     Source segment carrying the video.\r\n      --object-desc TEXT                SAM3 seed: carrier object English phrase.\r\n      --plane-desc TEXT                 Local plane English phrase.\r\n      --seed-time TEXT                  Seed frame time.\r\n      --initial-quad-json TEXT          Optional video-normalized TL/TR/BR/BL quad JSON derived from\r\n                                        verified mask evidence.\r\n      --duration-us INT                 Tracking window duration from the seed frame (us).\r\n      --output-dir TEXT REQUIRED        Directory for plane_quad output.\r\n      --channel <online|test|local_test> \r\n                                        Material request channel. Use `test` or `local_test` for internal\r\n                                        test resources.\r\n  -v, --version                         Show version information and exit.\r\n      --jq TEXT                         Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                                        .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                                        the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nWORKFLOW\r\n  build-runtime-manifest  strictly resolves package recipe steps into a standard runtime_data_manifest.\r\n  track-subject-mask / encode-subject-alpha / track-plane-quad are the atomic steps it dispatches; they can also be called directly.\r\n\r\nNOTE\r\n  Produces subject_alpha.v1 / subject_transform.v1 / plane_quad.v1 with time_base=draft_us (frame time_us rebased to 0). Apply via `draft effect add --type motiongraph --runtime-data-manifest <manifest>`.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Atomic: plane seed + in-memory video-tracking into plane_quad.v1\r\n(persist_to_file=false, no draft copy).\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h, --help                            Print this help message and exit\r\n      --ref TEXT                        Draft ref (standalone in-memory session; optional when the host\r\n                                        supplies an external editor session).\r\n      --target-seg-id TEXT REQUIRED     Source segment carrying the video.\r\n      --object-desc TEXT                SAM3 seed: carrier object English phrase.\r\n      --plane-desc TEXT                 Local plane English phrase.\r\n      --seed-time TEXT                  Seed frame time.\r\n      --initial-quad-json TEXT          Optional video-normalized TL/TR/BR/BL quad JSON derived from\r\n                                        verified mask evidence.\r\n      --duration-us INT                 Tracking window duration from the seed frame (us).\r\n      --output-dir TEXT REQUIRED        Directory for plane_quad output.\r\n      --channel <online|test|local_test> \r\n                                        Material request channel. Use `test` or `local_test` for internal\r\n                                        test resources.\r\n  -v, --version                         Show version information and exit.\r\n      --jq TEXT                         Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                                        .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                                        the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nWORKFLOW\r\n  build-runtime-manifest  strictly resolves package recipe steps into a standard runtime_data_manifest.\r\n  track-subject-mask / encode-subject-alpha / track-plane-quad are